  "reasons": [
    "Uncalibrated per-window 0.8 cutoff falsely excludes observed valid short/informal English. This is a selected diagnostic, not a population false-negative estimate.",
    "Whole-group quarantine also removes good paths when siblings fail; these intended group effects are distinct from direct language false exclusions.",
    "Only 2,688,887 content tokens counted once per raw train node remain; this is not a prepared or admitted 10M-position experiment. Do not silently inflate passes.",
    "Retain v1 unchanged as diagnostic evidence. Calibrate a separately versioned language policy on short/informal/full-context examples, and expand broader foundation text before the training freeze."
  ],
  "review_mode": "delegated_expert",
